Dear TC colleagues,

I'm expressing my interest in continuing as Chair through
the 2027.1 cycle. This past term I've tried to keep us
moving on the unglamorous work that doesn't get much attention
until it's missing, while staying honest with each other and
with the community about how and why we make decisions.

In this term, I'd like to push three things further.

First, the Contributor Experience Working Group exists now,
but isn't yet a functioning self-sustaining group. I want to
help it find its footing by recruiting community members
and getting it doing real work.

Second, I intend to finish refreshing the Technical Vision.
As we acknowledged, our vision hasn't been meaningfully
revisited in years. If elected, I'll see this through to a
ratification.

Third, I intend to keep us fully transparent and accountable,
to the community and to each other on this committee, even when
that means slowing down to explain ourselves or admitting we got
something wrong.

Thank you for your consideration!
